<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gustavo Petro</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1960">1960</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gustavo Petro is a Colombian politician who became Colombia's first left-wing president, serving from August 2022 to August 2026. A former member of the M-19 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> movement, he later served as a senator and as mayor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bogota">Bogotá</a> from 2012 to 2015. As president he pursued 'total peace' talks with armed groups and reforms of health care, labour and pensions.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gustavo-petro.jpg" alt="Gustavo Petro" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Departamento Nacional de Planeación · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Foto_Oficial_Presidente_Gustavo_Petro_(3x4_cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
